{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "02NI", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7911083d4f3da6e7d1075a6796ff2dbd8f73861bb2f9120e2a1454c8a092496f", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn general it is not possible to decompose a morphism\ninto its pieces where the relative dimension is a given\none. However, it is possible if the morphism has Cohen-Macaulay\nfibres and is flat of finite presentation.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6f9ab12f32541418bf971095ae0ad84dbeae4b601af81c8d39d5d44f0227ca5d", "unit_id": "tag:02NI:prose-0003"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "02NI", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\begin{slogan}\nCohen-Macaulay morphisms decompose into clopens of pure relative dimension\n\\end{slogan}", "MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$s \\in S$", "MATH_0005": "$X_s$", "MATH_0006": "$X_d \\subset X$", "MATH_0007": "$X = \\coprod_{d \\geq 0} X_d$", "MATH_0008": "$f|_{X_d} : X_d \\to S$", "MATH_0009": "$d$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{properties-definition-Cohen-Macaulay}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-flat-finite-presentation-CM-fibres-relative-dimension}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a0bab849b9f2157a2f9136f7c06eeef79b5a7058920331c9c41a175f9e9e8f75", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3e441f1e7ae791f264d2d84a3d92e64f94145bcf3e52f0950426dc5c25abcec3", "source_text": "<LOCKED_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes.\nAssume that\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0002> is flat,\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0003> is locally of finite presentation, and\n<STRUCT_0004> for all <MATH_0004> the fibre <MATH_0005> is Cohen-Macaulay\n(Properties, Definition <REF_0001>)\n<STRUCT_0005>\nThen there exist open and closed subschemes <MATH_0006>\nsuch that <MATH_0007> and <MATH_0008>\nhas relative dimension <MATH_0009>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a15d06a02415da4252034a5be876d89284d7fffd43c367e1db48773efe8dac90", "unit_id": "tag:02NM:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "02NI", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-relative-dimension-CM}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:494f85e19684a1bad5197826e1da3d169185650d9e188574557673e0001684c3", "source_text": "This is immediate from\nAlgebra, Lemma\n<REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:32640f2f5aac92343fcd7c5cd8e01a03e3873cd1be8667b3e2246e8606f63ca8", "unit_id": "tag:02NM:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "02NI", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$x \\in X$", "MATH_0004": "$s = f(x)$", "MATH_0005": "$f$", "MATH_0006": "$x$", "MATH_0007": "$\\dim_x(X_s) = 0$", "MATH_0008": "$f$", "MATH_0009": "$f$", "MATH_0010": "$0$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-locally-quasi-finite-rel-dimension-0}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:cac4a9bce8b72407b1fe176e1357aaaa7a476a0374bf72a33a41dd56a84d4061", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:92419f67f8c939865d4dc9451ecb3ddd86f8b70c7fd91c78724fccf5d4fa526e", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes.\nAssume <MATH_0002> is locally of finite type.\nLet <MATH_0003> with <MATH_0004>.\nThen <MATH_0005> is quasi-finite at <MATH_0006> if and only if <MATH_0007>.\nIn particular, <MATH_0008> is locally quasi-finite if and only if <MATH_0009> has relative\ndimension <MATH_0010>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:bb98f3df0b286e90c257eb230d35398657b13d1555775c572d938a98a4ee23c5", "unit_id": "tag:0397:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "02NI", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f$", "MATH_0002": "$x$", "MATH_0003": "$\\kappa(x)$", "MATH_0004": "$\\kappa(s)$", "MATH_0005": "$x$", "MATH_0006": "$X_s$", "MATH_0007": "$\\dim_x(X_s) = 0$", "MATH_0008": "$\\dim_x(X_s) = 0$", "MATH_0009": "$\\kappa(s) \\subset \\kappa(x)$", "MATH_0010": "$X_s$", "MATH_0011": "$x$", "MATH_0012": "$x$", "MATH_0013": "$f$", "MATH_0014": "$x$", "MATH_0015": "$X_s$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-residue-field-quasi-finite}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-quasi-finite-at-point-characterize}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-dimension-fibre-at-a-point}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-dimension-fibre-at-a-point}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{lemma-algebraic-residue-field-extension-closed-point-fibre}", "REF_0006": "\\ref{lemma-quasi-finite-at-point-characterize}", "REF_0007": "\\ref{lemma-finite-type-noetherian}", "REF_0008": "\\ref{lemma-quasi-finite-at-point-characterize}", "REF_0009": "\\ref{properties-lemma-isolated-dim-0-locally-noetherian}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a22af62d06f855fdad2d9d9e4e5cb8d64d0ca9b9c06d69d8b643af87630988a4", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:be8af18947214567d59cd9cdf72d4f676877f18f07ee7b19a4a4a1c755f3b866", "source_text": "First proof.\nIf <MATH_0001> is quasi-finite at <MATH_0002> then <MATH_0003> is a finite extension of\n<MATH_0004> (by\nLemma <REF_0001>)\nand <MATH_0005> is isolated in <MATH_0006> (by\nLemma <REF_0002>),\nhence <MATH_0007> by\nLemma <REF_0003>.\nConversely, if <MATH_0008> then by\nLemma <REF_0004>\nwe see <MATH_0009> is algebraic and\nthere are no other points of <MATH_0010> specializing to <MATH_0011>.\nHence <MATH_0012> is closed in its fibre by\nLemma <REF_0005>\nand by\nLemma <REF_0006> (3)\nwe conclude that <MATH_0013> is quasi-finite at <MATH_0014>.\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nSecond proof. The fibre <MATH_0015> is a scheme locally of finite type over a field,\nhence locally Noetherian (Lemma <REF_0007>).\nThe result now follows from\nLemma <REF_0008>\nand Properties, Lemma <REF_0009>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:bf1f3bff50e2e1fcddc4574ef58dfa8297221bf119ca4c9ec28a16da77655a4f", "unit_id": "tag:0397:proof"}
